+    Both namespaces sit behind default-deny in both directions, so a packet from A to B is
+    dropped unless A declares `egress: [B]` AND B declares `ingress_from: [A]`. Until
+    2026-09-07 nothing checked that, and llm carried exactly this defect: estate-db admitted
+    llm, llm never named estate-db, and the router could not roll -- every new pod died on
+    `httpx.ConnectError: All connection attempts failed` in Prisma's startup health check
+    while two pods older than the fence went on serving. The half-declaration reads like an
+    allowance in the file and is a deny on the wire, which is the worst kind of lie a fence
+    can tell. The one edge not graded is the one into SINK: policy_docs() grants every namespace
+    egress to the collector for LAW 50 whether it asked or not, so that half is never declared
+    and its absence proves nothing.
+    """
+    bad = []
+    for a, row in sorted(flows.items()):
+        for b in sorted(set(row.get("egress") or [])):
+            if b == SINK:
